<title>SWITZERLAND: SBC posts 1996 group net loss.</title>
<headline>SBC posts 1996 group net loss.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996.</p>
<p>				   (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net loss		 1,955	     vs profit 1,053</p>
<p>Group profit after tax and</p>
<p> before extraordinary items 1,328	     vs 1,053</p>
<p> Group operating profit     3,905	     vs 3,033</p>
<p> Minority participations    52		  vs 16</p>
<p>Note - Full name of Swiss banking group is Swiss Bank Corp (SBC). SBC last September forecast a 1.9 billion Swiss franc 1996 loss which would result from writeoffs totalling 3.3 billion francs.  </p>
<p>Group profit before extraordinary</p>
<p> items and taxes		1,560	     vs 1,342</p>
<p> Net interest income	  2,951	     vs 2,756</p>
<p> Net fee, commission income 4,374	     vs 3,337</p>
<p> Net trading income	   3,046	     vs 2,338</p>
<p> Net operating income	 10,751	    vs 8,877</p>
<p> Total operating expense    6,847	     vs 5,844</p>
<p> Personnel expenses	   4,228	     vs 3,692</p>
<p> Other expenses		 2,618	     vs 2,151</p>
<p>Provisions for doubtful debts</p>
<p> and contingencies	    1,350	     vs 1,005</p>
<p>Total depreciation, amortisation,</p>
<p> provisions		     2,345	     vs 1,691</p>
<p> Group assets vs yr earlier 359,945	   vs 288,276</p>
<p> Gross operating profit     3,905	     vs 3,033</p>
<p>    SBC Private Banking     1,296	     vs 1,088</p>
<p>    SBC Warburg		 1,025	     vs 663</p>
<p>    SBC Switzerland	   116 loss	  vs 182 loss</p>
<p>    SBC Brinson		 111		 vs 61</p>
<p>    Corporate Centre	  552 loss	  vs 288 loss</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
